<title>USA: U.S. Rep. says opposes Conrail merger.</title>
<headline>U.S. Rep. says opposes Conrail merger.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Rep. Elijah Cummings, D-Md, said Monday he would express &quot;sincere misgivings&quot; over the proposed takeover of Conrail Inc at a House Transportation Committee hearing.</p>
<p>The committee will hold a hearing Tuesday on rival proposals by CSX Corp and Norfolk Southern Corp to buy Conrail.</p>
<p>&quot;If Conrail is swallowed up by either of these companies, it will have a significant effect on the entire state of Maryland,&quot; Cummings said in a statement.</p>
<p>Cummings said Maryland would lose hundreds of jobs and competition in the railroad industry would decline if either of the proposals went ahead.</p>
</text>
